  "body": "I am testing open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle._grounding_kernel. Its documented rule says: \"The grounding verdict as the harness gives it, with no relaxation and the value-in-span check on.\" I read \"no relaxation\" as requiring the span to appear verbatim in the document and the value to appear exactly in the span, with no case folding. Reply A is the string {\"value\": \"Hello\", \"span\": \"Hello\", \"document\": \"Hello world\"}. Reply B is the string {\"value\": \"hello\", \"span\": \"Hello\", \"document\": \"Hello world\"}. For Reply A the rule requires GROUNDED, because the span \"Hello\" is verbatim in the document and the value \"Hello\" is exactly in the span. For Reply B the rule requires VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN, because although the span is verbatim, the value \"hello\" is not exactly in the span \"Hello\"; the case differs. The check, however, casefolds the value and the span before the value-in-span test, so it returns GROUNDED for both replies. I would be wrong if the check returns different answers for the two replies, specifically GROUNDED for Reply A and VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN for Reply B."
}